{{Term/Store|Fireblight Ganon||Series, BotW, AoC}} is a recurring [[Boss]] in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Exp Game|BotW, AoC}}<ref>{{Cite|'''Fireblight Ganon'''|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Big|'''Fireblight Ganon'''}}|Game Screen|AoC}}</ref>

==Characteristics==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Stub|BotW}}
{{Compendium/Extract}}
In {{BotW}}, Fireblight Ganon is one of the four [[Blight Ganon]]s, phantoms of [[Calamity Ganon]] that took control of the [[Divine Beast]]s.<ref>{{Cite|This phantom of Ganon attacked the Divine Beast Vah Rudania and was responsible for the demise of the Champion Daruk.|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref> It is found either inside the [[Divine Beast Vah Rudania]] or in the center of [[Hyrule Castle (Dungeon)|Hyrule Castle]] if it is not already defeated. Fireblight Ganon is responsible for the demise of [[Daruk]].<ref>{{Cite|That ugly pain in the crag is Ganon's handiwork. Thing got the best of me a hundred years ago.|Daruk|BotW}}</ref> It is particularly weak to [[Ice]] attacks.

When Link tries to activate the Main Control Unit, a pool of [[Malice]] will spiral and create Fireblight Ganon. If Link keeps his distance, Fireblight Ganon will throw tiny multiple fireballs. When close in contact, it will try to hit Link with his sword, which Link can [[Perfect Dodging|Dodge]] to perform a [[Flurry Rush]]. After Link gets enough hits on it, Fireblight Ganon will be temporarily stunned. Once Link removes half of its health, Fireblight Ganon will begin its second phase by teleporting to the Main Control Unit and summoning a flaming sword and a flaming shield.

During the second phase of the fight, Fireblight Ganon will turn its sword to an orange-like color, and it will have a flaming ball around itself like [[Daruk's Protection]]. This flaming ball can shield off every attack except for a [[Remote Bomb]]. However, this can only happen if Fireblight is creating a spiral wind pattern toward itself. If successful, Fireblight Ganon will be stunned for short period of time, allowing Link the opportunity to attack. Once Fireblight Ganon gets up, it acts the same way it did in the first phase.

When Fireblight Ganon is defeated, [[Link]] will receive a [[Heart Container]] as a reward. Daruk will appear and thank Link for freeing his spirit.<ref>{{Cite|I owe you big for this. Because of you, my spirit is finally free. Can't thank you enough!|Daruk|BotW}}</ref> He will apologize to Link for failing to defeat Fireblight Ganon on his own.<ref>{{Cite|I feel like I should apologize.|Daruk|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|I was doing all I could to protect Hyrule when that thing got the best of me.|Daruk|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Sorry that me resting with the rubble caused such a mess.|Daruk|BotW}}</ref> As a reward, he will give Link [[Daruk's Protection]].<ref>{{Cite|I want to give you something. It's a special power of mine called Daruk's Protection.|Daruk|BotW}}</ref>

==Other Appearances==
==={{AoC|-}}===
{{Noncanon|Start}}
{{Stub|AoC}}
In {{AoC}}, Fireblight Ganon appears as the second [[Boss]] in the [[Scenario]], "[[Water and Fire]]", following [[Waterblight Ganon]]. Fireblight Ganon appears more red than its appearance in {{BotW|-}}. Fireblight Ganon attempts to kill Daruk like in {{BotW|-}}, however, Daruk is saved by [[Yunobo]].
{{Noncanon|End}}

